Ms. Seo.

272
00:27:07,167 --> 00:27:09,670
You know that personal email usage
is prohibited at work, right?

273
00:27:10,796 --> 00:27:13,590
- Yes, sir.
- Why'd you break security protocol?

274
00:27:16,135 --> 00:27:17,636
I can't quite remember...

275
00:27:19,221 --> 00:27:21,682
Why are you asking me this?

276
00:27:30,524 --> 00:27:32,442
Oh, that's...

277
00:27:35,946 --> 00:27:39,700
Don't tell me
you're accusing me of being the spy.

278
00:27:42,286 --> 00:27:43,828
I swear it's not me.

279
00:27:43,829 --> 00:27:46,080
Me, a spy?
That's absolutely ridiculous!

280
00:27:46,081 --> 00:27:48,750
Spy or not, the dating scandal photos

281
00:27:49,418 --> 00:27:50,669
certainly look like your doing.

282
00:28:07,561 --> 00:28:08,770
This is for you.

283
00:28:13,400 --> 00:28:14,401
I'm sorry.

284
00:28:16,278 --> 00:28:17,321
What...

285
00:28:19,114 --> 00:28:21,909
Mr. Kang, could you
check this for me?

286
00:28:22,910 --> 00:28:26,121
You flat-out rejected
my feelings for you.

287
00:28:31,168 --> 00:28:32,752
- What?
- I don't need it.

288
00:28:32,753 --> 00:28:34,004
Then, buy me one.

289
00:28:37,382 --> 00:28:39,343
Then I saw you
meeting privately with Da-reum.

290
00:28:40,427 --> 00:28:41,428
It made me so mad.

291
00:28:44,890 --> 00:28:47,726
Some reporter handed me
a business card.

292
00:28:50,145 --> 00:28:53,315
- I had no idea it'd get this big.
- Ms. Seo.

293
00:28:54,024 --> 00:28:56,735
Are you aware of how much
this has cost the company?

294
00:28:58,528 --> 00:28:59,654
I'm so sorry.

295
00:28:59,655 --> 00:29:01,405
CEO KANG HA-GI

296
00:29:01,406 --> 00:29:03,033
You'll be disciplined
according to company policy.

297
00:29:03,700 --> 00:29:04,785
And...

298
00:29:07,037 --> 00:29:09,289
I suggest
you reflect on who truly deserves

299
00:29:10,791 --> 00:29:12,042
your apology.

300
00:29:50,080 --> 00:29:52,040
- Goodness.
- Good grief.

301
00:30:22,571 --> 00:30:25,866
- Oh, my. Thank you.
- I'm more grateful.

302
00:30:30,620 --> 00:30:32,497
I caught her thanks to your tip-off.

303
00:30:34,249 --> 00:30:37,669
I'm basically
a walking security camera, you know.

304
00:30:39,463 --> 00:30:42,715
Ms. Seo isn't the spy, though.
She just leaked the photos.

305
00:30:42,716 --> 00:30:43,884
Oh, really?

306
00:30:44,426 --> 00:30:46,887
Then, who is the real spy?

307
00:30:49,306 --> 00:30:51,975
Regardless, thank you for your help.

308
00:30:58,774 --> 00:31:01,693
Mr. Kang, I'll keep an eye out.

309
00:31:14,873 --> 00:31:16,041
Why, that little...

310
00:31:16,500 --> 00:31:19,002
I'm here to deliver fried chicken,
not take out the trash.

311
00:31:19,836 --> 00:31:23,673
Seriously, where on earth is Roy?

312
00:31:26,551 --> 00:31:27,844
QUICK DELIVERY
DRIVE SAFELY

313
00:31:28,512 --> 00:31:31,972
Jeez. Watch where you're going!

314
00:31:31,973 --> 00:31:33,016
Are you okay?

315
00:31:33,934 --> 00:31:36,061
Wait, this voice...

316
00:31:37,354 --> 00:31:38,522
Are you hurt?

317
00:31:39,106 --> 00:31:40,232
Roy?

318
00:31:43,985 --> 00:31:46,779
Oh, this is killing me. My back...

319
00:31:46,780 --> 00:31:48,907
Goodness, my hip.

320
00:31:49,449 --> 00:31:51,534
You're not even showing your face.

321
00:31:51,535 --> 00:31:53,160
Are you trying to pull a hit-and-run?

322
00:31:53,161 --> 00:31:56,039
A hit-and-run?
No, it's nothing like that.

323
00:31:56,790 --> 00:32:01,086
Then take off that helmet
and apologize properly.

324
00:32:07,509 --> 00:32:09,219
Take it off.

325
00:32:09,594 --> 00:32:11,138
Come on. Please take it off.

326
00:32:30,615 --> 00:32:32,868
I'm sorry. I was careless.

327
00:32:33,660 --> 00:32:34,744
I apologize.

328
00:32:35,537 --> 00:32:36,663
Here.

329
00:32:48,592 --> 00:32:50,427
What? Oh, thanks.

330
00:32:57,267 --> 00:32:59,685
Are you badly hurt?
Shall we go to the ER?

331
00:32:59,686 --> 00:33:02,438
No, I'm fine.

332
00:33:02,439 --> 00:33:03,565
- Are you okay?
- Yes.

333
00:33:06,776 --> 00:33:08,153
- You can let go now.
- Right.

334
00:33:14,576 --> 00:33:17,037
The brand HAN is really fascinating.

335
00:33:17,579 --> 00:33:20,206
The Creative Director's identity is
under wraps.

336
00:33:20,207 --> 00:33:22,917
All they have on social media is
their brand account.

337
00:33:22,918 --> 00:33:25,378
I think that's what piques
everyone's curiosity.

338
00:33:27,172 --> 00:33:29,882
That's enough for now.
Let's go eat. I'm starving.

339
00:33:29,883 --> 00:33:32,092
- Good idea.
- Yes, let's eat.

340
00:33:32,093 --> 00:33:33,844
Do you see this, everyone?

341
00:33:33,845 --> 00:33:34,930
What does it look like?

342
00:33:35,472 --> 00:33:38,558
I have the corporate credit card
in my hands.

343
00:33:39,100 --> 00:33:41,810
- What do you want to eat?
- Budae-jjigae.

344
00:33:41,811 --> 00:33:44,271
- Budae-jjigae? Let's go eat, then.
- Great.

345
00:33:44,272 --> 00:33:46,232
Let's go. Let's go downstairs.

346
00:33:46,233 --> 00:33:47,483
- Budae-jjigae.
- What else?

347
00:33:47,484 --> 00:33:50,110
Spicy stir-fried webfoot octopus.

348
00:33:50,111 --> 00:33:52,531
- Come on. Let's go.
- Gosh...

349
00:33:57,369 --> 00:34:00,038
- Da-reum, you coming?
- Yes. I am.

350
00:34:22,811 --> 00:34:23,937
She's an outcast.

351
00:34:24,479 --> 00:34:26,690
She brought it on herself.

352
00:34:37,909 --> 00:34:38,994
Ms. Seo.

353
00:34:39,619 --> 00:34:41,663
Can I have a word?

354
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:46,126
Okay.

355
00:34:51,256 --> 00:34:53,550
What was that?
Are they having a fight?

356
00:35:06,605 --> 00:35:07,606
Ms. Seo.

357
00:35:08,773 --> 00:35:09,899
What do you want?

358
00:35:13,987 --> 00:35:16,781
What are you doing?
Are you going to beat me up?

359
00:35:19,618 --> 00:35:23,163
No, wait, sorry. I'm really sorry.

360
00:35:37,177 --> 00:35:39,929
Don't you have anything to say to me?

361
00:35:44,392 --> 00:35:45,393
I'm sorry.

362
00:35:48,271 --> 00:35:50,023
I really am.

363
00:35:51,483 --> 00:35:52,734
I must've lost my mind.

364
00:35:55,070 --> 00:35:57,697
Thanks to you, I ended up
submitting a written apology

365
00:35:58,990 --> 00:36:00,700
and becoming an outcast.

366
00:36:01,785 --> 00:36:04,829
I know I deserve
what I'm going through.

367
00:36:06,581 --> 00:36:08,792
I'm having such a hard time
that I just want to quit.

368
00:36:11,002 --> 00:36:12,128
I know.

369
00:36:13,088 --> 00:36:14,547
Been there, done that.

370
00:36:17,342 --> 00:36:20,970
If we don't make up,
things won't get better for you.

371
00:36:23,932 --> 00:36:25,974
So what?

372
00:36:25,975 --> 00:36:27,477
Are you going to be the bigger person

373
00:36:28,436 --> 00:36:30,563
and forgive me or something?

374
00:36:31,815 --> 00:36:32,816
Not yet.

375
00:36:34,567 --> 00:36:35,568
But

376
00:36:36,986 --> 00:36:39,114
I will hold out a helping hand.

377
00:36:41,241 --> 00:36:43,284
If you actually feel bad

378
00:36:45,328 --> 00:36:46,621
will you help me?

379
00:36:49,749 --> 00:36:50,834
What?

380
00:36:51,876 --> 00:36:53,545
How can I help you?

381
00:36:54,504 --> 00:36:56,463
The HAN TFT proposal.

382
00:36:56,464 --> 00:36:59,217
It's way too hard for me.
You've written loads of proposals.

383
00:37:00,635 --> 00:37:02,011
Let's work on it together.

384
00:37:05,724 --> 00:37:06,808
Together?

385
00:37:07,267 --> 00:37:08,309
Yes.

386
00:37:12,313 --> 00:37:13,314
Sure. Whatever.

387
00:37:52,812 --> 00:37:55,148
Welcome.
Take your time to look around.

388
00:37:56,566 --> 00:37:58,567
- Can you take a look?
- Okay.

389
00:37:58,568 --> 00:38:01,070
Who's the director in charge
of this store?

390
00:38:01,613 --> 00:38:04,866
Oh, that would be
our Director Lee Chan.

391
00:38:08,286 --> 00:38:09,954
- I'll take this.
- Okay.

392
00:38:10,330 --> 00:38:11,956
You can pay over there.

393
00:38:33,603 --> 00:38:34,813
Let's meet up.

394
00:38:35,396 --> 00:38:36,439
Stop avoiding me.

395
00:38:47,283 --> 00:38:49,410
Are you Lee Chan?

396
00:38:54,582 --> 00:38:55,625
Han Jeong-yeon?

397
00:38:57,627 --> 00:38:58,962
- Let's talk another time.
- Okay.

398
00:39:03,049 --> 00:39:04,384
It really is you.

399
00:39:09,597 --> 00:39:11,057
When did you get to Korea?

400
00:39:13,101 --> 00:39:14,269
Just a few days ago.

401
00:39:15,436 --> 00:39:18,314
Has it been 15 years
since we last met?

402
00:39:20,483 --> 00:39:22,235
You never called once.

403
00:39:24,320 --> 00:39:25,655
Did you miss me?

404
00:39:31,077 --> 00:39:32,412
I remember the old days.

405
00:39:32,787 --> 00:39:34,664
They were the good times.

406
00:39:35,623 --> 00:39:38,042
You and I used to listen
to music at school.

407
00:39:39,836 --> 00:39:41,086
Do you remember?

408
00:39:41,087 --> 00:39:45,090
We promised to go to a jazz bar
for some live music and whiskey

409
00:39:45,091 --> 00:39:46,926
when you turned 20.

410
00:39:47,176 --> 00:39:49,137
You weren't there when I turned 20.

411
00:39:53,558 --> 00:39:54,684
I'm sorry about that.

412
00:39:57,562 --> 00:39:59,439
But I missed you guys, though.

413
00:40:02,191 --> 00:40:03,192
"You guys"?

414
00:40:04,569 --> 00:40:05,612
You and Ha-gi.

415
00:40:11,117 --> 00:40:12,201
Is he well?

416
00:40:13,661 --> 00:40:15,330
You two were inseparable.

417
00:40:16,664 --> 00:40:18,583
You haven't changed at all.

418
00:40:19,417 --> 00:40:22,045
- How so?
- How you make me uncomfortable.

419
00:40:26,716 --> 00:40:29,218
I thought becoming a celebrity
would've made you cool.

420
00:40:30,345 --> 00:40:31,429
You haven't changed either.

421
00:40:37,602 --> 00:40:40,313
I'm staying at the boutique hotel
across the road.

422
00:40:41,898 --> 00:40:43,024
See you again soon.

423
00:41:03,544 --> 00:41:06,965
You're incredibly good with a knife.

424
00:41:08,591 --> 00:41:10,218
I used to go by the nickname

425
00:41:10,468 --> 00:41:12,053
"Seocho's Knife-man."

426
00:41:14,097 --> 00:41:17,183
The stench of blood back then...

427
00:41:21,688 --> 00:41:23,523
"Knife-man"?

428
00:41:25,149 --> 00:41:26,650
That's in the past.

429
00:41:26,651 --> 00:41:28,861
Now I'm everyone's punching bag.

430
00:41:30,530 --> 00:41:33,449
Was he disowned for having a record?

431
00:41:34,117 --> 00:41:36,911
So what's your ideal type, Mi-mi?

432
00:41:38,955 --> 00:41:40,957
My ideal type?

433
00:41:41,541 --> 00:41:43,960
I like competent and capable men

434
00:41:45,420 --> 00:41:46,504
who are good kissers.

435
00:41:54,137 --> 00:41:56,305
That's a very clear answer.

436
00:41:56,931 --> 00:41:57,932
That's me.

437
00:42:06,524 --> 00:42:09,652
- I need to go to the ladies' room.
- Sure.

438
00:42:22,623 --> 00:42:23,750
My heart's racing.

439
00:42:27,045 --> 00:42:28,087
She wants to kiss already?

440
00:42:29,714 --> 00:42:31,132
That's way too fast.

441
00:42:32,341 --> 00:42:34,093
He looks incompetent.

442
00:42:36,429 --> 00:42:37,764
I bet he's a lousy kisser.

443
00:42:45,521 --> 00:42:47,231
Okay. Then what?

444
00:42:48,441 --> 00:42:49,650
You don't have a knife.

445
00:42:51,319 --> 00:42:53,196
How about we go
with kidnap and confinement?

446
00:42:53,988 --> 00:42:55,364
Murder is too much.

447
00:42:56,657 --> 00:42:59,368
Jeez. That's tricky.

448
00:43:01,954 --> 00:43:04,415
Something urgent came up.

449
00:43:04,832 --> 00:43:06,374
I have to dash.

450
00:43:06,375 --> 00:43:08,461
Mi-mi!

451
00:43:10,171 --> 00:43:11,547
Hold on, Mi-mi.

452
00:43:12,298 --> 00:43:13,841
Why is he following me?
Now I'm scared.

453
00:43:14,842 --> 00:43:16,719
What got into her? Mi-mi.

454
00:43:17,762 --> 00:43:19,680
Darn it.

455
00:43:26,771 --> 00:43:28,481
- I need help.
- With what?

456
00:43:28,815 --> 00:43:30,399
Someone's chasing me.

457
00:43:33,402 --> 00:43:34,695
My stomach hurts.

458
00:43:36,489 --> 00:43:38,449
You forgot your coat.

459
00:43:41,911 --> 00:43:43,371
ATTORNEY KIM MIN-WOO

460
00:43:44,580 --> 00:43:45,581
TRUE

461
00:43:49,001 --> 00:43:53,255
I don't know what you mistook me for,
but I really am an attorney.

462
00:43:53,256 --> 00:43:55,340
You know the state my body's in.

463
00:43:55,341 --> 00:44:00,428
What thug would have tech neck,
rounded shoulders, or a slipped disc?

464
00:44:00,429 --> 00:44:03,056
Why didn't you say so from the start?

465
00:44:03,057 --> 00:44:05,017
You never asked.

466
00:44:05,184 --> 00:44:06,519
It's not a good look

467
00:44:06,894 --> 00:44:09,730
to brag about your job
when no one asked.

468
00:44:20,491 --> 00:44:22,243
Does this look right?

469
00:44:22,535 --> 00:44:26,247
I wish we could add
a little something.

470
00:44:29,750 --> 00:44:30,793
Can you excuse me?

471
00:44:34,755 --> 00:44:36,089
Ms. Seo.

472
00:44:36,090 --> 00:44:38,467
This is my initial draft.

473
00:44:39,427 --> 00:44:40,428
How does it look?

474
00:44:45,558 --> 00:44:46,726
Oh, well...

475
00:44:47,310 --> 00:44:52,023
Page one makes the first impression,
and this looks too ordinary.

476
00:44:52,940 --> 00:44:55,234
It's always good
to put the conclusion first.

477
00:44:56,819 --> 00:44:58,029
In that case...

478
00:45:07,371 --> 00:45:08,372
This part...

479
00:45:08,623 --> 00:45:11,083
You two are working hard together.

480
00:45:17,465 --> 00:45:18,925
- Do this first.
- Okay.

481
00:45:19,175 --> 00:45:20,258
Then this.

482
00:45:20,259 --> 00:45:21,635
- Three, one, two?
- Yes.

483
00:45:21,636 --> 00:45:22,845
Okay. Got it.

484
00:45:43,991 --> 00:45:45,743
Let's go home, everyone.

485
00:45:46,661 --> 00:45:48,078
- Marketing Team.
- Yes?

486
00:45:48,079 --> 00:45:49,829
Look at the time.
Why are you still here?

487
00:45:49,830 --> 00:45:51,832
I still have work to do.

488
00:45:56,921 --> 00:45:58,965
You've got the gist of it.
You just need to fix the details.

489
00:45:59,215 --> 00:46:01,384
Finish it up tomorrow.
Rest is crucial for work.

490
00:46:01,634 --> 00:46:04,512
- Go on home.
- Can you review my proposal, too?

491
00:46:09,684 --> 00:46:11,977
- Go home.
- What? It's that perfect?

492
00:46:11,978 --> 00:46:14,146
You can't finish this today.
Do it over tomorrow.

493
00:46:15,481 --> 00:46:17,524
Okay, everyone. Pack up and go home.

494
00:46:17,525 --> 00:46:19,318
- Go home.
- But...

495
00:46:19,902 --> 00:46:21,278
- Bye.
- See you.

496
00:46:21,279 --> 00:46:23,071
- Let's all go home.
- Go home.

497
00:46:23,072 --> 00:46:24,948
- Okay.
- Go on home.

498
00:46:24,949 --> 00:46:26,617
- Good job, guys.
- Let's go.

499
00:46:28,202 --> 00:46:29,370
Finish it tomorrow.

500
00:46:59,859 --> 00:47:01,652
You can't really cook, can you?

501
00:47:01,986 --> 00:47:03,321
Well...

502
00:47:04,613 --> 00:47:06,490
I guess so.

503
00:47:06,782 --> 00:47:09,242
- I can't...
- I can't cook many things

504
00:47:09,243 --> 00:47:11,037
but I make a mean pasta.

505
00:47:12,788 --> 00:47:13,956
Do you?

506
00:47:14,332 --> 00:47:15,833
All you have to do is

507
00:47:16,792 --> 00:47:18,127
heat the bottled sauce
and add the pasta.

508
00:47:34,935 --> 00:47:35,936
Ms. Da-reum.

509
00:47:36,854 --> 00:47:37,980
Shall we swap tasks?

510
00:47:38,439 --> 00:47:39,482
Why?

511
00:47:39,648 --> 00:47:41,525
I'm really bad with knives.

512
00:47:41,984 --> 00:47:44,570
What? Step aside, then.
I'll take over.

513
00:48:32,076 --> 00:48:33,119
It's good.

514
00:48:33,536 --> 00:48:38,249
- You're great at cooking pasta.
- Right? I told you so.

515
00:48:38,749 --> 00:48:40,793
Eat at my place next time.

516
00:48:42,211 --> 00:48:44,004
At your place?

517
00:48:45,423 --> 00:48:47,842
The thing I'm second best at cooking

518
00:48:48,300 --> 00:48:49,676
is tteokbokki.

519
00:48:49,677 --> 00:48:50,761
We should have that next time.

520
00:48:54,098 --> 00:48:55,141
Okay, let's do that.

521
00:49:10,739 --> 00:49:11,740
So...

522
00:49:13,284 --> 00:49:15,035
You knew it was Ms. Seo.

523
00:49:16,412 --> 00:49:17,496
Why didn't you say so?

524
00:49:23,419 --> 00:49:26,547
I didn't want to suspect
for no good reason.

525
00:49:28,048 --> 00:49:29,925
You could've gone to anyone else

526
00:49:30,843 --> 00:49:32,261
for help with your proposal.

527
00:49:34,096 --> 00:49:35,764
I told you once before.

528
00:49:37,516 --> 00:49:38,601
I used to be an outcast.

529
00:49:43,272 --> 00:49:44,982
Looking at Ms. Seo made me think

530
00:49:46,150 --> 00:49:48,444
about how tormented she must feel.

531
00:49:49,945 --> 00:49:52,823
And also so lonely.

532
00:49:55,951 --> 00:49:57,703
That's what came to my mind first.

533
00:49:59,663 --> 00:50:00,998
I didn't want to see her...

534
00:50:04,627 --> 00:50:06,086
go through what I did.

535
00:50:07,922 --> 00:50:09,089
Ms. Da-reum.

536
00:50:11,258 --> 00:50:12,843
Despite being hurt yourself

537
00:50:13,844 --> 00:50:15,721
you choose to console others.

538
00:50:21,435 --> 00:50:24,313
That's what you did for me.

539
00:50:31,695 --> 00:50:32,821
Actually...

540
00:50:34,615 --> 00:50:36,116
I've lived my life
doing the opposite.

541
00:50:37,993 --> 00:50:40,579
I did my best
not to get too close to anyone.

542
00:50:42,623 --> 00:50:44,458
It's because
whenever I cherished someone...

543
00:50:49,838 --> 00:50:51,006
they ended up leaving me.

544
00:50:53,259 --> 00:50:54,260
It was easier...

545
00:50:56,178 --> 00:50:58,556
to throw myself into my work.

546
00:51:01,308 --> 00:51:02,434
You managed

547
00:51:03,686 --> 00:51:05,062
to break through that wall
to get to me.

548
00:51:29,253 --> 00:51:31,797
Do you remember this wine?

549
00:51:32,631 --> 00:51:35,968
Yes, it's the bottle I gifted you.

550
00:51:38,137 --> 00:51:39,221
The wine that helps

551
00:51:40,598 --> 00:51:41,682
one's love come true.

552
00:51:47,479 --> 00:51:48,522
It actually worked.

553
00:52:08,500 --> 00:52:09,834
MISSED CALL: HA-GI

554
00:52:09,835 --> 00:52:12,338
HA-GI: PLEASE PICK UP

555
00:52:43,327 --> 00:52:46,121
APPELLO KANG HA-GI

556
00:52:48,832 --> 00:52:54,755
CEO KANG'S LEADERSHIP
SHINES THROUGH SCANDAL

557
00:53:39,258 --> 00:53:40,718
Why was it Ha-gi?

558
00:53:43,387 --> 00:53:44,388
What do you mean?

559
00:53:45,180 --> 00:53:46,598
You chose him.

560
00:53:49,435 --> 00:53:51,145
Why Ha-gi and not me?

561
00:54:00,571 --> 00:54:01,989
It was us first.

562
00:55:04,176 --> 00:55:05,385
We met first.

563
00:55:06,345 --> 00:55:07,429
We connected first.

564
00:55:08,138 --> 00:55:09,181
Hey, catch.

565
00:55:29,243 --> 00:55:30,702
Whenever you smiled

566
00:55:31,578 --> 00:55:33,372
I thought I was the reason
you were smiling.

567
00:55:49,054 --> 00:55:50,055
So why

568
00:55:52,057 --> 00:55:53,892
did you choose Ha-gi in the end?

569
00:56:05,320 --> 00:56:06,405
Tell me.

570
00:56:09,783 --> 00:56:10,826
The look in your eyes.

571
00:56:12,202 --> 00:56:13,495
It's the same as back then.

572
00:56:17,916 --> 00:56:20,002
You always wanted to rescue me.

573
00:56:22,170 --> 00:56:23,505
I felt grateful

574
00:56:25,090 --> 00:56:26,258
but I also hated it.

575
00:56:32,639 --> 00:56:33,640
Why?

576
00:56:35,017 --> 00:56:36,393
Your pity.

577
00:56:37,686 --> 00:56:39,187
You look at me
like I was unfortunate.

578
00:56:41,565 --> 00:56:42,816
Ha-gi didn't.

579
00:56:46,111 --> 00:56:47,279
He liked me...

580
00:56:49,281 --> 00:56:50,866
for who and what I was.

581
00:56:52,242 --> 00:56:53,911
I felt at ease around him.

582
00:56:58,874 --> 00:57:00,918
I thought
if I were with someone I like

583
00:57:01,376 --> 00:57:04,046
I'd be able to share
my feelings with him

584
00:57:04,546 --> 00:57:07,716
by laughing, crying

585
00:57:09,134 --> 00:57:11,261
whining, and even fighting.

586
00:57:12,387 --> 00:57:14,473
But for some reason

587
00:57:16,266 --> 00:57:17,267
I couldn't easily do that

588
00:57:18,894 --> 00:57:20,479
with you.

589
00:57:34,284 --> 00:57:37,454
Did something happen
between you and Ha-gi?

590
00:57:45,504 --> 00:57:46,588
No.

591
00:57:47,339 --> 00:57:49,716
I shouldn't have come. Take care.

592
00:57:50,425 --> 00:57:51,426
Chan.

593
00:57:57,224 --> 00:57:58,850
Do you need my help?

594
00:58:25,502 --> 00:58:28,588
See if you can win Ha-gi's heart.

595
00:59:00,871 --> 00:59:02,789
They never even called us back

596
00:59:03,040 --> 00:59:04,916
but they met up with SE Corporation.

597
00:59:06,418 --> 00:59:08,419
We lost out this time.

598
00:59:08,420 --> 00:59:09,671
Darn it.

599
00:59:18,764 --> 00:59:21,141
HAN DIDN'T CREATE A BRAND
BUT AN AESTHETIC

600
00:59:25,479 --> 00:59:26,938
Shall we return to the hotel?

601
00:59:27,647 --> 00:59:31,485
No, we have one more place to go.

602
00:59:32,778 --> 00:59:34,780
CEO KANG HA-GI

603
00:59:39,493 --> 00:59:41,578
Mr. Kang.

604
00:59:42,412 --> 00:59:45,040
HAN's CEO is coming to visit Appello.

605
00:59:46,208 --> 00:59:48,292
- What?
- HAN, the brand.

606
00:59:48,293 --> 00:59:49,836
They're on their way.

607
01:00:08,355 --> 01:00:10,899
- Are they here?
- Yes.

608
01:01:05,912 --> 01:01:08,498
Meet HAN's CEO, Ms. Han Jeong-yeon.

609
01:01:12,335 --> 01:01:13,336
It's a pleasure.

610
01:01:13,837 --> 01:01:15,672
Welcome to Appello.

611
01:01:28,018 --> 01:01:30,687
Nice to meet you, Mr. Kang Ha-gi.

612
01:01:52,751 --> 01:01:56,338
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

613
01:02:07,474 --> 01:02:10,185
EPILOGUE

614
01:02:37,879 --> 01:02:39,630
Now, the five-second countdown.

615
01:02:39,631 --> 01:02:40,882
No, three seconds.

616
01:02:41,174 --> 01:02:44,970
- Three, two, one.
- Three, two, one.

617
01:02:47,097 --> 01:02:48,806
So about that.

618
01:02:48,807 --> 01:02:51,141
- The slides.
- Move the table here.

619
01:02:51,142 --> 01:02:52,726
- That should work.
- Okay.

620
01:02:52,727 --> 01:02:54,604
- That looks better.
- Right?

621
01:02:55,272 --> 01:02:56,731
- Yes.
- I think it's too big.

622
01:03:07,826 --> 01:03:10,703
They might as well broadcast
that they're dating.

623
01:03:10,704 --> 01:03:13,289
Right? They say when a couple
starts dating at work

624
01:03:13,290 --> 01:03:14,833
everyone knows about it,
even the water cooler.

625
01:03:30,098 --> 01:03:33,517
WITNESS 1

626
01:03:33,518 --> 01:03:34,727
Let's start the meeting.

627
01:03:34,728 --> 01:03:35,895
- Okay.
- Okay.

628
01:03:38,773 --> 01:03:40,065
ROMANTIC NIGHT VIEW SPOTS IN SEOUL

629
01:03:40,066 --> 01:03:41,234
SEOUL NIGHT DATE IDEAS

630
01:03:42,902 --> 01:03:44,195
WITNESS 2

631
01:03:48,241 --> 01:03:49,784
WITNESS 3

632
01:03:54,998 --> 01:03:57,917
STORAGE

633
01:04:04,632 --> 01:04:08,260
Da-reum, Ms. Kim needs the sample
urgently. Have you found it?

634
01:04:08,261 --> 01:04:09,428
What?

635
01:04:09,429 --> 01:04:12,265
- Yes, I'm bringing it now.
- Okay.

636
01:04:20,482 --> 01:04:22,691
Let's pretend we have no idea.

637
01:04:22,692 --> 01:04:24,277
They're both clueless
when it comes to dating.

638
01:04:28,031 --> 01:04:29,281
- You're excited.
- Why are you so happy?

639
01:04:29,282 --> 01:04:31,326
It gives me butterflies.

640
01:04:31,868 --> 01:04:33,203
Haven't you ever been
in a relationship?

641
01:04:35,330 --> 01:04:37,748
Han Jeong-yeon?
She's Ha-gi's first love.

642
01:04:37,749 --> 01:04:41,752
If you ever make my Da-reum cry...

643
01:04:41,753 --> 01:04:43,421
The person who wrote that proposal...

644
01:04:43,797 --> 01:04:45,924
Would you like to lead the project?

645
01:04:46,466 --> 01:04:47,759
Why Ms. Da-reum of all people?

646
01:04:48,259 --> 01:04:49,552
Whatever it may be

647
01:04:50,178 --> 01:04:53,264
I want you to do
what your heart tells you to do.

648
01:04:53,598 --> 01:04:56,350
Does my relationship
with Mr. Kang bother you?

649
01:04:56,351 --> 01:05:00,396
- But I trust the person I'm dating.
- Do you?

650
01:05:00,397 --> 01:05:01,439
What does that mean?

651
01:05:01,564 --> 01:05:05,068
I want Ha-gi back.

652
01:05:06,069 --> 01:05:08,738
Were you with her all this while?
